<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ibrahim II of Karaman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1464</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Karamanoğlu İbrahim Bey</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ibrahim II was ruler of the Karamanid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beylik</a> in south-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> from 1424 to 1464. He fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> repeatedly, often allied with crusaders and other Turkish rivals, and built mosques and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrasa">madrasas</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karaman">Karaman</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konya">Konya</a>. After his death his sons fought over the succession, opening the way for the Ottoman conquest.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ibrahim-ii-of-karaman.jpg" alt="Ibrahim II of Karaman" width="320" height="184" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gold_dirhem_Ibrahim_II_Karamanid.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
